{"seq":15,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r5","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T01:08:22.863Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"76dc1e933e4a43518a61896ba2fb74aacfe8c3b037d3a6a5f0f108da44142fb0","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#coastal-team","text":"@Bettina, here is the list of tickets and feature requests for Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL) and Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF), from #coastal-team, #coastal-random and the Coastal notes. Pellow Home Living is left out.\n\nPellucid Harbor Logistics\n- #4419: Yard_Dwell_Summary report times out when filtered by container length. Open per Moss's cheat sheet. The 11/2/2025 digest also cites #4419 for a barge slip 7 schedule sync, which sounds like DMF. Please confirm which it is.\n- PD-8841: Gate 4B chassis pool holds on double-booked gates. Source: your Dec 2025 cutover recap.\n- Not ticketed: chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change (the main friction point in the cheat sheet).\n\nDriftmoor Marine Freight\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges (from warehouse managers, per the cheat sheet).\n- Not ticketed: tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B. Engineering gave a manual CSV patch for the night dispatcher.\n- Not ticketed: patched manifest CSV requested before the 06:00 shift (11/2/2025 digest). I can't see whether it was delivered.\n- Barge slip 7 schedule sync (11/2/2025 digest). See the #4419 note above.\n\nNot included: PD-4821, PD-4824, PD-4827 and #8812 belong to Pellow Home Living or Saltmarsh Provisions, not PHL or DMF."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
